- Unix paths

Since this is intended for our enterprise development team, Windows support is important.

13. PERFORMANCE

Measure indexing performance.

Do not make unsupported performance claims.

Add a benchmark or test fixture demonstrating:

first index

versus

incremental index with only a few changed files.

14. FAILURE BEHAVIOR

If the index is corrupt:

- do not crash the MCP server
- report the problem
- rebuild safely when possible

If indexing fails for one file:

- do not necessarily fail the entire repository index
- record the failure
- continue processing other files
- expose indexing warnings

15. LOGGING

Do not log source contents.

Do not log secrets.

Support verbose diagnostics.

16. DOCUMENTATION

